## Outcome

Add a purpose-bound hosted-development qualification-run root whose manifest owns every synthetic
descendant; issue only `qualification:write` credentials for those descendants; enforce the
development boundary in both application and database state; exclude qualification records from
every operational view; and expose them only in a separate authenticated Qualification Runs view.

Implement expiry that preserves lineage, exact preview-bound purge with stale/foreign/production
refusals, and retained tombstones. After the controls pass, run QH-009 and structurally faithful
QH-010 replays through the shared hosted-development namespace from the Linux and Windows
development fixtures without borrowing operational credentials.

## Completion Gate

The exact candidate passes focused model/service/API/UI tests, database constraint and refusal
tests, operational absence checks, authenticated qualification-view checks, expiry and purge
lineage checks, retained-tombstone checks, and QH-009/QH-010 hosted-development replays from both
disposable operating-system fixtures. The web, Linux, and Windows development lanes contain that
candidate; production remains unchanged.

## Completion Evidence

`work/evidence/evidence-lifecycle-qualification-m4.md` records exact candidate
